<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Žabljak Crnojevića</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Žabljak Crnojevića is a ruined fortified town on a rocky hill near the north-western shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-skadar">Lake Skadar</a> in Montenegro. It was the seat of the Crnojević rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a> in the fifteenth century until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-crnojevic">Ivan Crnojević</a>, under Ottoman pressure, moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetinje">Cetinje</a> in 1482. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> then held it until Montenegro took it in 1878.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zabljak-crnojevica.jpg" alt="Žabljak Crnojevića" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zabljak_1860_c.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
